Parent: 1377

## Context

Author-approved split of 1377. Deferred until a concrete consumer need and
actual CLI/version capability evidence justify structured constraints; this
is not a scheduled implementation. Sibling 1464 independently finishes raw
failure evidence. Provider API support alone does not establish CLI support.

Relevant existing surfaces: `scripts/gaze_seat.py`, `scripts/seat_clock.py`,
`skills/route/routes.json` and `tests/test_gaze_seat.py`.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] A versioned structured-report request is independent of Arena/product
  scoring and carried only through doors with evidenced actual CLI syntax
  and behavior. Provenance records requested mode, CLI/door version evidence,
  and passed/unsupported/unverified status; unknown is not native support.
- [ ] Native grammar/strict schema, JSON syntax mode and prompt-only request
  remain distinguishable. Unsupported/degraded behavior is visible in the
  plan or report; a parseable response alone is not constrained generation.
- [ ] REVIEWED/FINDINGS/ESCALATE and review-note records remain authoritative:
  validation cannot clear invalid, missing or contradictory review content.
  Reach declarations remain declarations unless separately bound to verified
  tool evidence. Existing raw-evidence retention/provenance and credential
  protection remain intact.
- [ ] Offline stub/fixture tests cover unsupported/degraded paths, ignored
  requests, malformed/missing fields and a positive passthrough only if a
  real door option has been established. The verified-supported set may be
  empty: then report unsupported and make no native-support claim.
- [ ] Applicable gaze seat tests/project checks pass. No live model/API
  calls, consent/author-hold, cross-family spend or scoring-policy changes
  are made.
